<p><strong>My logicking, may be bullshit:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>If the suits and the cells are perceived to be women, then the idea of wearing them or containing people inside them would be abhorrent, not form part of the containment procedures.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Allison Eckhart, as in SCP-2565 herself, already contains herself, because she contains the organs, skin cells, blood and brains of Allison Eckhart: all of which reduce themselves to Allison Eckhart via the logic of the skip.</p>
<p>Since the Site Director is also an Allison Eckhart themselves, and the staff using the HAZMAT suits are Allison Eckharts, there would be nothing unusual to either Allison Eckhart, because Allison Eckhart has been containing Allison Eckharts ever since the initial anomaly manifested.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>deepest Allison Eckharts</p>
</blockquote>
<p>In this case, we replace &quot;Allison Eckhart&quot; with &quot;regret&quot;. Allison Eckhart can embody &quot;regret&quot;, or &quot;fear&quot; or &quot;joy&quot; much like a political figure can embody &quot;hope&quot; or &quot;grief&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>100 liters of Allison Eckhart</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Liters are admittedly more frequently used to describe liquids as opposed to people, but what would this imply about the <em>state</em> of Allison Eckhart?</p>
<p>Would you want to drink a human being pulped into 100 liters of juice like so much CapriSun?</p>

